; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;">Effective mentor training for teachers goes beyond simply pairing a veteran educator with a newcomer; it focuses on developing the specific&nbsp;<span data-path-to-node="0" data-index-in-node="140" style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;">coaching and other skill sets</span>&nbsp;required to support another professional’s growth.&nbsp;</div><div style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;"><br style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;"></div><div style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;">Let us know how you enjoyed the training!</div>', NULL, 5, 1, 0, NULL, '2026-05-12 19:23:23', '2026-05-12 19:35:53', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'standard'),
  (5, 'test-staff-only-columns-a27fad0b', 'Test Staff Approval', 'published', 'This collection is to test the Staff Only columns.', 'General', 4, '2026-05-27', '/images/placeholder-cover.svg', NULL, NULL, NULL, 21, 0, 0, NULL, '2026-05-27 12:18:25', 'Aug 14 2026  5:58AM', 2, NULL, '{"enabled":true,"stages":[{"id":"stage-ihlxewajeyh","name":"Stage 1","approvalMode":"all","assignees":[{"type":"role","value":"reviewer"}],"conditions":null,"reminderAfterHours":24,"escalationAfterHours":72,"escalationAssignees":null}]}', NULL, NULL, 'standard'),
  (6, 'credit-by-demonstrated-mastery-cdm-814f762f', 'Credit by Demonstrated Mastery (CDM)', 'published', 'Students who are ready to earn high school credit by showing what they know, without taking the course, can apply for Credit by Demonstrated Mastery (CDM).', 'General', 5, NULL, 'data:image/png;base64,', 'https://resources.finalsite.net/images/v1747849462/wcpssnet/hftgawk1qsknmcaafdky/wcpss_logos_rgbAsset141.svg', '<div><b>Welcome to the CDM Application!</b></div><div><br></div><div><b>Step 1: Submit Your CDM Application</b></div><div>Students interested in earning credit through CDM must submit the CDM Application and Agreement to their school’s CDM coordinator.</div><div><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">Deadline: Typically in September or October.</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;"><br></span></div><div><b>Step 2: Meet with Your School Counselor</b></div><div>Before testing, students will meet with a counselor to:</div><div>Understand how CDM affects their transcript, GPA, and class rank</div><div>Review how CDM fits into their four-year graduation plan</div><div>Timing: Most counseling takes place November–January, depending on the testing schedule.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Step 3: Take the Phase 1 Assessment</b></div><div>Phase 1 is a multiple-choice exam that measures core knowledge of the course standards.</div><div><br></div><div>Testing Window: Final five days of first semester</div><div>Results Shared: January–February</div><div>If You Pass: You’ll receive instructions to begin Phase 2.</div><div>If You Do Not Pass: The CDM process ends.</div><div>Important Note: This attempt will not appear on your transcript.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Step 4: Complete the Phase 2 Assessment</b></div><div>Phase 2 measures how well you can apply your knowledge. You may be asked to:</div><div><br></div><div>Complete a task aligned to course standards such as an assessment, portfolio, or artifact.&nbsp;</div><div>Submissions Due: By end of March</div><div>Results Shared: In April by a district CDM Review Panel</div><div>If You Pass: Credit will be added to your transcript with the label CDM—no letter grade is assigned.</div><div>If You Do Not Pass: No credit is awarded, and there’s no record on your transcript.</div><div><br></div><div>CDM Available Courses&nbsp;</div><div>The courses below are those available for the Credit by Demonstrated Mastery (CDM) process for the 2025-26 school year. Included is the type of assessment and minimum score required for Phase 1.</div><div><br></div><div>English I, locally-developed exam, 90%&nbsp;</div><div>English II, EOC, level V Scale Score ≥ 565</div><div>NC Math 1, EOC,&nbsp; level V Scale Score ≥ 563</div><div>NC Math 2, locally-developed exam, 90%</div><div>NC Math 3, EOC, level V Scale Score ≥ 563</div><div>Biology, EOC, level V Scale Score ≥ 361</div><div>Spanish, French, German, Proficiency Exam, Novice High</div><div>Career and Technical Education CDM Courses</div><div>Career and Technical Education (CTE) requires completion of CTE State Assessments with minimum score of 90%. Students may only apply for courses that are offered at their school.&nbsp;&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>BB40 Business Management I</div><div>BF21 Financial Planning I</div><div>GS11 Project Management I</div><div>FI21 Interior Design Fundamentals</div><div>FN41 Food and Nutrition I</div><div>HU40 Health Science I</div>', NULL, 18, 1, 0, NULL, '2026-05-28 13:25:14', '2026-06-10 18:46:19', 33, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'standard'),
  (7, 'second-collection-test-cbdc9f0c', 'Document Preview Test', 'published', 'This is a collection for testing', 'General', 4, NULL, '/images/placeholder-cover.svg', NULL, 'This is a collection for testing the Ticket System.<div><br></div><div>Also, we are testing the new Document Viewer!</div>', NULL, 14, 1, 0, NULL, '2026-05-30 15:00:10', 'Aug 14 2026  5:58AM', 2, NULL, '{"enabled":true,"stages":[{"id":"stage-p5c6q52jbf","name":"Stage 1","approvalMode":"any","assignees":[{"type":"role","value":"team_manager"},{"type":"role","value":"reviewer"}],"conditions":null,"reminderAfterHours":24,"escalationAfterHours":72,"escalationAssignees":null}]}', NULL, NULL, 'standard'),
  (8, 'intent-to-apply-for-grant-e3e6cec9', 'Intent to Apply for Grant', 'published', 'Please fill out the form below for applying for a grant. Please wait 24-36 hours for us to get back to you. Thank you!', 'General', 8, NULL, '/api/collections/public/intent-to-apply-for-grant-e3e6cec9/cover-photo', 'https://resources.finalsite.net/images/v1747849462/wcpssnet/hftgawk1qsknmcaafdky/wcpss_logos_rgbAsset141.svg', '<span style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;">***PLEASE NOTE: &nbsp;ONLY PRINCIPALS OR SCHOOL GRANT CONTACTS MAY COMPLETE THIS FORM.*** </span><div><span style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;"><br></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;">Principals and School Grant Contacts should log into their WCPSS Google accounts to complete and as partially form. Please be sure to have all the needed information ready as partially completed forms cannot be saved. *** &nbsp;For a preview, visit </span><a href="https://goo.gl/e8Yr9g" style="color: rgb(11, 87, 208); text-decoration: underline; font-family: Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;">https://goo.gl/e8Yr9g</a><div style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;">&nbsp;</div><div style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;">To ensure that WCPSS policies are followed, please work with your Principal or School Grant Contact to submit this form for each grant you plan to pursue, answering the questions to the best of your ability. WCPSS Board approval is required for all grant submissions, and the Office of Grants will manage the approval process for you. Please do not submit a grant until you receive notification from the Office of Grants that the funding opportunity is Board approved. Be sure to keep a file of all your grant materials, including this Intent to Apply form, your proposal, budget, and any other relevant materials.</div><div style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;">***<b>PLEASE DO NOT SUBMIT THIS FORM FOR <a href="https://wakeconnect.wcpss.net/sites/communications/News/75769/new-guidelines-for-teachers-using-online-classroom-wish-lists" style="color: rgb(11, 87, 208); text-decoration: underline;">ONLINE CLASSROOM WISHLISTS</a> SUCH AS AMAZON, ETC</b>.***&nbsp; <br><br>Questions? Visit our <a href="https://wakeconnect.wcpss.net/sites/grants/SitePage/1583/grants" style="color: rgb(11, 87, 208); text-decoration: underline;">website</a>&nbsp;for additional information, or email us at <a href="mailto:grants@wcpss.net" style="color: rgb(11, 87, 208); text-decoration: underline;">grants@wcpss.net</a>.<br><br>Per Board Policy 8100 - The budget resolution shall conform to the uniform budget format (GS115C-426) established by the State Board of Education. &nbsp;WCPSS Budget Resolution adopted October 7, 2014 (page 30, B1-4).<br><br>If information changes after the form is submitted, please contact us (<a href="mailto:grants@wcpss.net" style="color: rgb(11, 87, 208); text-decoration: underline;">grants@wcpss.net</a>) to update the information. </div></div>', NULL, 17, 1, 0, NULL, '2026-06-01 18:46:09', '2026-06-10 18:45:43', 34, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'standard'),
  (9, 'test-collection-f5b4487b', 'Test Collection', 'published', 'This is a test collection. Select "Edit Form" to view details. You can create as many collections as needed for your organization; there is no limit. Responses can be Authenticated or Anonymous, and all collection forms are mobile friendly! The link to the survey is under the Share tab.', 'General', 11, NULL, '/api/collections/public/test-collection-f5b4487b/cover-photo', 'https://resources.finalsite.net/images/v1747849462/wcpssnet/hftgawk1qsknmcaafdky/wcpss_logos_rgbAsset141.svg', '<div><b>Welcome!</b></div>You can add detailed instructions for your collection as needed here. Add multiple fields and pages under Questions. Attachments are not functional in demo mode.<div><div><br></div><div><b>What is a "Ticket"?</b></div><div>A ticket is a way for internal staff to keep track of notes for each submission in a collection. Just like a form, you can design a ticket to hold the fields you need for your team to keep track of information after the submission. Once you have a Ticket set up you can assign it from the "Add Ticket" section in your collection.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><b>Adding information for a submission</b></div><div>To add information to a submission, click on Records &gt; Individual &gt; Select a Submission. You can leave a Comment, or if a Ticket is assigned to the collection, you can fill in the fields created for the Ticket. You can also add a "Staff Only" field type. "Staff Only" field types are only viewable by staff and show under the submitted item.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Approvals</b></div><div>If you need someone to approve a submission, you can enable Approvals and assign a Person or Role. Approvals are currently in development.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Seed Data</b></div><div>To add sample data for a collection, go to Settings &gt; Seed Data.</div></div><div><br></div><div><div style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;"><span style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ; font-weight: bolder;">Adding additional staff</span></div><div style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;">Any WCPSS staff member can use this application. If you want to restrict them to certain aspects of the application, give them the Reviewer role. A Reviewer cannot edit a collection. This may be expanded to different types of Roles in the future.</div></div><div style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;"><br></div><div style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;"><b>Staff Only Fields</b></div><div style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;">Columns marked as "Staff Only" as only visible by staff, and can be accessed from Records &gt; Individual &gt; View submission.</div>', NULL, 20, 1, 0, NULL, '2026-06-09 18:04:18', 'Aug 25 2026  1:45AM', 340, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 'standard'),
  (11, 'fall-2026-conferences-9b150d96', 'Fall 2026 Conferences', 'published', 'This is a test of the slot collection type. See Collections > Add Collection.', NULL, 11, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 23, 0, 0, NULL, '2026-06-23 13:55:54', '2026-07-08 13:59:34', 340, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'signup_sheet'),
  (12, 'test-collection-51df3f71', 'Test Collection #2', 'published', 'This is a test collection. Select "Edit Form" to view details. You can create as many collections as needed for your organization; there is no limit. Responses can be Authenticated or Anonymous, and all collection forms are mobile friendly! The link to the survey is under the Share tab.', 'General', 11, '2026-08-12', '/images/placeholder-cover.svg', 'https://resources.finalsite.net/images/v1747849462/wcpssnet/hftgawk1qsknmcaafdky/wcpss_logos_rgbAsset141.svg', '<div><b>Welcome!</b></div>You can add detailed instructions for your collection as needed here. Add multiple fields and pages under Questions. Attachments are not functional in demo mode.<div><div><br></div><div><b>What is a "Ticket"?</b></div><div>A ticket is a way for internal staff to keep track of notes for each submission in a collection. Just like a form, you can design a ticket to hold the fields you need for your team to keep track of information after the submission. Once you have a Ticket set up you can assign it from the "Add Ticket" section in your collection.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><b>Adding information for a submission</b></div><div>To add information to a submission, click on Records &gt; Individual &gt; Select a Submission. You can leave a Comment, or if a Ticket is assigned to the collection, you can fill in the fields created for the Ticket. You can also add a "Staff Only" field type. "Staff Only" field types are only viewable by staff and show under the submitted item.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Approvals</b></div><div>If you need someone to approve a submission, you can enable Approvals and assign a Person or Role. Approvals are currently in development.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Seed Data</b></div><div>To add sample data for a collection, go to Settings &gt; Seed Data.</div></div><div><br></div><div><div style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;"><span style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ; font-weight: bolder;">Adding additional staff</span></div><div style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;">Any WCPSS staff member can use this application. If you want to restrict them to certain aspects of the application, give them the Reviewer role. A Reviewer cannot edit a collection. This may be expanded to different types of Roles in the future.</div></div><div style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-