  (7398, 6, 10, 'qnb6kep6w08', 'multiple_choice', 'Course Request (max 3)', NULL, 2, 0, '["English I, locally-developed exam, 90% ","English II, EOC, level V Scale Score ≥ 565","NC Math 1, EOC,  level V Scale Score ≥ 563","NC Math 2, locally-developed exam, 90%","NC Math 3, EOC, level V Scale Score ≥ 563","Biology, EOC, level V Scale Score ≥ 361","Spanish, French, German, Proficiency Exam, Novice High","BB40 Business Management I","BF21 Financial Planning I","GS11 Project Management I","FI21 Interior Design Fundamentals","FN41 Food and Nutrition I","HU40 Health Science I"]', 'radio', NULL, 8, 0, 0),
  (7399, 6, 10, '269ser8x131', 'comment', '<div><b>I understand this assessment will include a two-phase process.</b></div><div><br></div><div><b>Phase 1 </b>will include an examination to establish my mastery of the foundational skills and content that this course requires.&nbsp;&nbsp;</div><div>I must earn a minimum score on Phase 1 to move forward to Phase 2.&nbsp; The minimum score for each type of assessment is as follows:&nbsp;</div><div>90% for a locally-developed exam</div><div>90% for a CTE Post-Assessment</div><div>Novice High for World Language Assessments</div><div>Level V on an EOC</div><div>I have one attempt at the exam.</div><div>Prior to the exam, I may review the content standards for the course or subject. Standards can be found at this link: http://www.ncpublicschools.org/curriculum/</div><div>If I earn the appropriate score, I will move onto Phase 2.&nbsp; If not, I will not have the opportunity to earn CDM for this course. Results of Phase 1 cannot be appealed.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><b>In Phase 2</b>, I will participate in an assessment that reflects a deep understanding of the content standards, including the ability to apply the skills and knowledge expected at the end of the course.&nbsp; Phase 2 may require a presentation, project, on-demand writing, performance assessment, or interview as evidence of my abilities.</div><div>The CDM Review Panel will determine if I have demonstrated mastery of the course content and skills.&nbsp; If I am successful, I will get credit for the course which will appear on my transcript as “CDM.”&nbsp; No grade or quality points will be granted; this process will have no impact on my GPA. Appeals for unsuccessful attempts on Phase 2 must be submitted to the school based CDM coordinator, in writing, within 10 school days of notification of results.</div><div>I understand that I will meet with my school’s CDM Coordinator to discuss the process and long-term implications.</div>', NULL, 3, 0, NULL, 'radio', NULL, 9, 0, 0),
